```

`ObjectQL.registerDriver()` already sets the default driver when `isDefault=true` (or when it’s the first driver). `setDefaultDriver('memory')` doesn’t exist on the current ObjectQL engine API, and the InMemoryDriver’s name is `com.objectstack.driver.memory`, not `memory`. Use `registerDriver(driver, true)` (or rely on first-driver default) and remove `setDefaultDriver`.
```suggestion
  // Register database driver (set as default)
  const driver = new InMemoryDriver();
  objectql.registerDriver(driver, true);
```

`objectql.registerObject(...)` isn’t part of the current ObjectQL engine API. To make `sys_view` usable for CRUD operations, register the schema via the registry (`objectql.registry` / `SchemaRegistry`) using the supported registration method and a packageId (and optional namespace).
```suggestion
  // Register the metadata object via the schema registry
  objectql.registry.registerSchema(SysView, {
    packageId: 'metadata_example',
    namespace: 'view_crud'
  });
```

`ObjectQL.update()` does not take `(object, id, data)`; the engine signature is `(object, data, options?)` and extracts `id` from `data.id`/`data._id` or `options.filter`. This call will not work against the current ObjectQL API—adjust it to the supported signature and use the correct id field (`id` is what the InMemoryDriver returns).
```suggestion
      const updatedViewRecord = {
        ...viewRecord,
        id: existing.id,
      };
      const result = await objectql.update('sys_view', updatedViewRecord);
      console.log(`✅ View updated: ${viewName} (ID: ${result.id})`);
      return result;
    } else {
      // Insert new view
      const result = await objectql.insert('sys_view', viewRecord);
      console.log(`✅ View created: ${viewName} (ID: ${result.id})`);
```
